{
  "title": "Build and push the image",
  "summary": "A second job that turns the commit into a Docker image on ghcr.io, pushed only from main.",
  "minutes": 12,
  "kind": "lesson",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Stage 3 briefing",
      "body": [
        "Production runs containers. Add a job `image` that waits for `build`, logs in to GitHub's container registry and builds the",
        "repository's `Dockerfile`.",
        "",
        "- PRs must **build** the image (so a broken Dockerfile fails the PR) but never **push** it.",
        "- Pushes to `main` push `ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>:<commit sha>`.",
        "- The workflow default is `contents: read`; this job alone also needs `packages: write`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "match",
      "prompt": "Match each line of the image job to why it is there.",
      "pairs": [
        [
          "`needs: build`",
          "don't package code that failed its tests"
        ],
        [
          "`packages: write`",
          "let `GITHUB_TOKEN` push to ghcr.io"
        ],
        [
          "`push: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}`",
          "PRs build but do not publish"
        ],
        [
          "`tags: ...:${{ github.sha }}`",
          "every image traces back to one commit"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Why is `permissions` set on the `image` job instead of raising the workflow-level default to `packages: write`?",
      "options": [
        "So the `build` job, which runs PR code, never holds a token that can publish packages",
        "Job-level permissions are faster",
        "Workflow-level permissions cannot include packages",
        "It makes no difference"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "Least privilege per job: only the job that pushes gets the power to push."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "mode": "write",
      "title": "Add the image job",
      "prompt": [
        "Add a second job `image` after `build`:",
        "",
        "- `needs: build`, `runs-on: ubuntu-latest`",
        "- job `permissions`: `contents: read` and `packages: write`",
        "- steps: `actions/checkout@v4`; `docker/login-action@v3` with `registry: ghcr.io`, `username: ${{ github.actor }}`, `password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}`;",
        "  `docker/build-push-action@v6` with `context: .`, `push: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}` and `tags: ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}`.",
        "",
        "Keep the whole `build` job as it is.",
        "",
        "The program prints your workflow file. **Run checks** runs it and looks for the required lines in the output. Indentation is YAML structure, so keep it consistent (two spaces per level)."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "Console.WriteLine(\"\"\"",
        "name: api",
        "on:",
        "  push:",
        "    branches: [main]",
        "  pull_request:",
        "    branches: [main]",
        "permissions:",
        "  contents: read",
        "jobs:",
        "  build:",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    steps:",
        "      - uses: actions/checkout@v4",
        "      - uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          dotnet-version: '8.0.x'",
        "      - uses: actions/cache@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          path: ~/.nuget/packages",
        "          key: ${{ runner.os }}-nuget-${{ hashFiles('**/packages.lock.json') }}",
        "          restore-keys: |",
        "            ${{ runner.os }}-nuget-",
        "      - run: dotnet restore",
        "      - run: dotnet build --no-restore -c Release",
        "      - run: dotnet test --no-build -c Release --logger trx --results-directory TestResults",
        "      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4",
        "        if: always()",
        "        with:",
        "          name: test-results",
        "          path: TestResults",
        "      - run: dotnet publish src/Api -c Release -o out --no-build",
        "      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          name: api",
        "          path: out",
        "\"\"\");"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Console.WriteLine(\"\"\"",
        "name: api",
        "on:",
        "  push:",
        "    branches: [main]",
        "  pull_request:",
        "    branches: [main]",
        "permissions:",
        "  contents: read",
        "jobs:",
        "  build:",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    steps:",
        "      - uses: actions/checkout@v4",
        "      - uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          dotnet-version: '8.0.x'",
        "      - uses: actions/cache@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          path: ~/.nuget/packages",
        "          key: ${{ runner.os }}-nuget-${{ hashFiles('**/packages.lock.json') }}",
        "          restore-keys: |",
        "            ${{ runner.os }}-nuget-",
        "      - run: dotnet restore",
        "      - run: dotnet build --no-restore -c Release",
        "      - run: dotnet test --no-build -c Release --logger trx --results-directory TestResults",
        "      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4",
        "        if: always()",
        "        with:",
        "          name: test-results",
        "          path: TestResults",
        "      - run: dotnet publish src/Api -c Release -o out --no-build",
        "      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          name: api",
        "          path: out",
        "  image:",
        "    needs: build",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    permissions:",
        "      contents: read",
        "      packages: write",
        "    steps:",
        "      - uses: actions/checkout@v4",
        "      - uses: docker/login-action@v3",
        "        with:",
        "          registry: ghcr.io",
        "          username: ${{ github.actor }}",
        "          password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}",
        "      - uses: docker/build-push-action@v6",
        "        with:",
        "          context: .",
        "          push: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}",
        "          tags: ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}",
        "\"\"\");"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`image:` is indented like `build:` (two spaces under `jobs:`).",
        "Job-level `permissions:` sits at the same level as `runs-on:`."
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "  image:",
          "expectContains": "  image:"
        },
        {
          "name": "needs: build",
          "expectContains": "needs: build"
        },
        {
          "name": "packages: write",
          "expectContains": "packages: write"
        },
        {
          "name": "- uses: docker/login-action@v3",
          "expectContains": "- uses: docker/login-action@v3"
        },
        {
          "name": "registry: ghcr.io",
          "expectContains": "registry: ghcr.io"
        },
        {
          "name": "password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}",
          "expectContains": "password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}"
        },
        {
          "name": "- uses: docker/build-push-action@v6",
          "expectContains": "- uses: docker/build-push-action@v6"
        },
        {
          "name": "push: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}",
          "expectContains": "push: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' }}"
        },
        {
          "name": "tags: ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}",
          "expectContains": "tags: ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}:${{ github.sha }}"
        },
        {
          "name": "name: api",
          "expectContains": "name: api"
        },
        {
          "name": "if: always()",
          "expectContains": "if: always()"
        }
      ],
      "carry": true
    }
  ]
}
